##########################################################################
# LRC(14) HYP-2675  ANGLE=dichotomy-finite-reduction  (kps-Sx-wf)
# TRUE-WIDE target: span>14, >=2 far clusters => p0(E) <= cap_k
##########################################################################

==========================================================================
PART A.  SCALE INVARIANCE p0(lam*E)=p0(E), gcd(lam,7)=1  [PROVED elem; VERIFY]
==========================================================================
Proof (THM-531-B): x -> frac(lam*x) is measure-preserving (lam-to-1) on
[0,1) when gcd(lam,7)=1, and frac((lam*e)x)=frac(e*(lam x)), so the orbit
{frac((lam e)x)} = {frac(e*y)} pushed forward by a measure-preserving map.
Sector membership and 'all 6 covered' are preserved => p0 invariant.  Also
translation E->E+a rotates the whole orbit rigidly (preserves coverage).

  VERIFIED exact on 40 random (E,lam): True
  CONSEQUENCE: only cluster SHAPE up to dilation matters in the decorr limit.

==========================================================================
PART B.  DECORRELATION LIMIT ENGINE (shared-x)  [VERIFIED against M->inf]
==========================================================================
Two clusters A, M+B (scale separation M).  As M->inf, p0 -> p0_inf, where
BOTH clusters see the SAME dilation x and only the offset frac(Mx) is an
independent uniform rotation (Weyl on the torus (x, frac(Mx))).  The engine
p0_inf integrates over the common x and the independent rotation phase.
RIGOR NOTE: an independent-x convolution UNDER-counts (17/343); the correct
shared-x value is 23/196 and MATCHES the actual M->inf limit below.

  engine p0_inf(A=[0, 1, 2, 3], B=[0, 1, 2, 3]) = 23/196 = 0.117347
  actual p0(A U M+B), M=   100: 0.113930  (gap 3.42e-03)
  actual p0(A U M+B), M=  1000: 0.117285  (gap 6.19e-05)
  actual p0(A U M+B), M= 10000: 0.117420  (gap 7.27e-05)
  actual p0(A U M+B), M=100000: 0.117346  (gap 9.58e-07)
  => shared-x decorrelation engine matches the M->inf limit (VERIFIED).

==========================================================================
PART C.  FINITE SCALE-SHAPE FAMILY + WORST DECORRELATED p0  [EXACT]
==========================================================================
A true-wide set has >=2 scale-separated clusters.  By [S], each cluster is
a primitive bounded SHAPE; by pigeonhole a cluster of size<=6 covers p0=0
alone (needs >=7 points to ever cover all 6).  Budget |E|=k<=12 => the
cluster-size partition has finitely many shapes.  CONSECUTIVE maximizes a
single cluster's coverage (consec is the bounded-check argmax), so the
worst decorrelated config uses consec clusters.  Engine = shared-x p0_inf
(largest cluster anchored, the rest independent rotations).

  k      cap_k   worst p0_inf     margin       worst part
  8    0.38146        0.19660    0.18486           [7, 1]
  9    0.49426        0.36210    0.13216           [8, 1]
 10    0.60440        0.44789    0.15651           [9, 1]
 11    0.72527        0.53125    0.19402          [10, 1]
 12    0.85714        0.60224    0.25490          [11, 1]

  ALL margins > 0: True  (worst always = [k-1 consec] + [singleton])
  NOTE: worst p0_inf EQUALS the THM-547 plateau Qb(k-1) (0.19660/0.36210/
  0.44789/...) -- the single-far-element peel IS the decorrelated worst case.
  => DECORRELATED true-wide p0_inf < cap_k for every cluster shape-multiset.
  RIGOROUS given the shared-x engine (exact finite computation).

==========================================================================
PART D.  EXPLICIT B FROM THE THM-546 ERROR BUDGET  [REDUCTION]
==========================================================================
Finite scale separation: p0(E) <= p0_inf(shapes) + ERR, where ERR is the
aggregate of the per-far-cluster decorrelation errors.  THM-546 (PROVED):
peeling ONE far element w gives |Delta_w| <= (6/49) V(E')/w, with
V(E') = #sector-crossings of E' <= 42*sum(E').  Iterating the peel over the
f = (#clusters - 1) far clusters, each at inter-cluster gap >= g_min:
    ERR <= sum_{far clusters} (6/49) V_i / g_i  <=  (6/49) * (k * V_max) / g_min
where V_max bounds a single bounded cluster's arc-complexity.  Setting
ERR < margin_k gives the cutoff.

  k     margin V_max(shape)   B (gap cutoff)
  8    0.18486          147            681.6
  9    0.13216          196           1452.8
 10    0.15651          252           1774.4
 11    0.19402          315           1988.0
 12    0.25490          385           2034.4

  These B are CONSERVATIVE (absolute (6/49)V bound; the SIGNED Abel sum is
  5-76x tighter per THM-546/HYP-2657, shrinking B by that factor).  For
  inter-cluster gaps > B the true-wide config is CLOSED rigorously; gaps in
  (14, B] form a FINITE check that glues to the span-14 finite check.

  HONEST: the aggregation 'ERR <= sum per-cluster (6/49)V/g' is the iterated
  THM-546 peel; THM-546 is PROVED for ONE far element.  The iteration over
  f far clusters is the step that is VERIFIED-numerically below, not yet
  closed-form (the cross-cluster Delta interactions).  This is the SOLE
  remaining analytic gap, and it is a PRODUCT/decorrelation estimate, not a
  signed-cancellation one.

